k to which wires are swapped.\n\n  // Even better: use structural analysis bit by bit.\n\n  // Let me build a helper to trace the expected structure and find deviations.\n\n  // First, let's identify all the roles gates should play:\n  // For bit i, the expected gates are:\n  //   PS_i (partial sum): XOR(xi, yi) -> some wire\n  //   Z_i: if i==0, PS_0 outputs z0; else XOR(PS_i_out, carry_i) -> zi\n  //   G_i (generate): AND(xi, yi) -> some wire\n  //   P_i (propagate): AND(PS_i_out, carry_i) -> some wire (only if i>0)\n  //   C_i (carry out): if i==0, G_0; else OR(G_i, P_i) -> some wire\n\n  // Since wires are swapped (output labels wrong), we need to match gates to roles\n  // based on their INPUT structure, not output labels.\n\n  // Approach: for each gate, determine what role it plays based on inputs,\n  // then check if its output label is consistent.\n\n  // Gate classification by inputs:\n  // - Inputs are (xi, yi): must be PS_i (XOR) or G_i (AND)\n  // - One input from PS_i, one from carry: Z_i (XOR) or P_i (AND)\n  // - Inputs from G_i and P_i: C_i (OR)\n  // - One input from PS_i, one from G_j/P_j: need more analysis\n\n  // Let me take a different approach. I'll trace the carry chain.\n  // At bit 0, we know the inputs are x00 and y00.\n  // The gate with inputs x00,y00 and op=XOR should output z00.\n  // The gate with inputs x00,y00 and op=AND should output carry_0.\n\n  // For bit i>0:\n  // Find gate with inputs xi,yi and op=XOR -> this is PS_i, its output is partial_sum_i\n  // Find gate with inputs xi,yi and op=AND -> this is G_i\n  // Find gate with inputs (partial_sum_i, carry_{i-1}) and op=XOR -> this is Z_i, should output zi\n  // Find gate with inputs (partial_sum_i, carry_{i-1}) and op=AND -> this is P_i\n  // Find gate with inputs (G_i_out, P_i_out) and op=OR -> this is C_i, carry_i = C_i_out\n\n  // With swaps, the \"should output zi\" check fails. But the gate STRUCTURE (op + inputs)\n  // is unchanged - only the output label is wrong.\n\n  // So: trace the carry chain using gate structure (ignoring output labels),\n  // then for each gate, check if its output label matches the expected role.\n  // Mismatches indicate swapped wires.\n\n  // Let me build a map from input pair to gate(s), keyed by sorted input pair + op\n\n  function gateKey(in1: string, in2: string, op: string): string {\n    return [in1, in2].sort().join(',') + ':' + op;\n  }\n\n  // Map from (sorted inputs, op) to gate\n  const gatesByInputs = new Map<string, Gate[]>();\n  for (const g of gates) {\n    const key = gateKey(g.in1, g.in2, g.op);\n    if (!gatesByInputs.has(key)) gatesByInputs.set(key, []);\n    gatesByInputs.get(key)!.push(g);\n  }\n\n  // Trace carry chain\n  let carryWire: string | null = null;\n  const suspectWires: string[] = [];\n\n  for (let i = 0; i <= N; i++) {\n    const xi = `x${String(i).padStart(2, '0')}`;\n    const yi = `y${String(i).padStart(2, '0')}`;\n    const zi = `z${String(i).padStart(2, '0')}`;\n\n    if (i === 0) {\n      // Bit 0: half adder\n      // XOR(x0, y0) -> z00\n      const xorKey = gateKey(xi, yi, 'XOR');\n      const xorGates = gatesByInputs.get(xorKey);\n      if (xorGates && xorGates.length > 0) {\n        const g = xorGates[0];\n        if (g.out !== zi) {\n          suspectWires.push(g.out, zi);\n        }\n      }\n\n      // AND(x0, y0) -> carry\n      const andKey = gateKey(xi, yi, 'AND');\n      const andGates = gatesByInputs.get(andKey);\n      if (andGates && andGates.length > 0) {\n        carryWire = andGates[0].out;\n      }\n\n      if (i === N) {\n        // Only 1 bit - carry becomes z01\n        // Handled below\n      }\n    } else if (i === N) {\n      // Final bit: carry becomes zN\n      // The carry wire should be zN\n      // But the gate producing carryWire is some OR gate (or AND for bit 0 carry)\n      // The output label of that gate should be zN\n      // Actually, carry is already a wire. If carryWire != zN, then\n      // the gate that outputs carryWire has